        "eyebrow": "Why it exists",
        "heading": "A Woman Remembered",
        "body": "<p>Some women have a way of staying with you.</p><p>Perhaps it's the way they enter a room, how they remember the smallest details, or the particular perfume that lingers long after they've left.</p><p>It feels like a handwritten letter tucked into a handbag. An unexpected compliment from a stranger. The perfume your grandmother wore, if she'd had a standing reservation downtown and a rather interesting past.</p><p>Familiar, but never predictable. For ordinary Tuesdays, extraordinary evenings, and everything in between.</p>",
        "drop_cap": true,
        "pull_quote": "Some women leave a room. Others leave a story.",
        "anchor": "the-story"
      }
    },
